From a6f4b72f06193985645b543e831240d993859bbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Blackwellboy <76774064+Blackwellboy@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 06:46:03 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 17/20] lanes: TF_FILL_CUT_IN=T lets a prompt of at most T
 tokens run between another pass's pieces (off by default)

A prompt pass ran whole, or in TF_FILL_CHUNKS pieces only while other streams decoded, and nothing was admitted
until it ended: a short request sent behind a 64K-token prompt waited out the whole pass (28-36 s on two GB10s).

With TF_FILL_CUT_IN set (and TF_FILL_CHUNKS), every pass runs in pieces, also with no stream decoding, and between
two pieces the host admits the first queued request whose prompt is at most T tokens and has no images. Its pass
runs whole there; the paused pass then resumes from its next chunk. The dsv41 backend keeps the paused pass and
resumes it with a fill_resume frame, so both ranks' model views return to its slot and extent (its rows, rings and
ids stay in its own slot meanwhile). Unset, nothing changes.

(cherry picked from commit 16701b487a8e1c695a31fdd7cba2af72a3b9c6e2)
